OL,3,GNEWSAMan finishes 62-mile cricket
OL,4,Arun-up record attempt
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man has finished a Guinness World
OL,7,FRecord attempt for the longest run-up
OL,8,Fprior to bowling a cricket ball.
OL,10,FSam Bodoano, from Worplesdon, near
OL,11,FGuildford in Surrey, ran 62 miles
OL,12,F(100km), starting at Lord's Cricket
OL,13,FGround in north London on Saturday and
OL,14,Ffinishing by bowling a game's opening
OL,15,Fball to his father at Valley End
OL,16,FCricket Club in Woking on Sunday.
OL,18,FThe run took 14 hours and raised almost
OL,19,F#6,000 for cancer charity The Ruth
OL,20,FStrauss Foundation.
OL,23,APub: 01-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,328,320,200,140,0,100
